-### Monocular Depth Scale Alignment
-**Definition:** A post-optimization step to resolve the up-to-scale problem in 3D scenes reconstructed from multi-view images by aligning the scale of optimized 3D Gaussians with metric-scale monocular depth estimates [S2, unofficial].
-**Pitfall:** Unlike original 3DGS, this method avoids pruning initial COLMAP points to prevent affecting the distribution of optimized Gaussian parameters, ensuring fair comparison with other studies [S2, unofficial]. It optimizes a global scene scale factor $a$ to minimize the L1 difference between inverse monocular depth and rendered inverse depth [S2, unofficial].
